    Reactotron para Debug

https://docs.infinite.red/reactotron/quick-start/react-native/?_gl=1*1gwmhi7*_ga*MTE0MDU4NzE5Mi4xNzQ5MDUxNTMx*_ga_37GXT4VGQK*czE3NTI4ODQxMDYkbzc2JGcxJHQxNzUyODg2MDc1JGo2MCRsMCRoMA..

Baixar o programa:
https://github.com/infinitered/reactotron/releases/tag/reactotron-app%403.7.7

agora a 2° etapa:
npm i --save-dev reactotron-react-native

e cria o arquivo: ReactotronConfig.js na raiz do projeto:
    
    import Reactotron from "reactotron-react-native";

    Reactotron.configure() // controls connection & communication settings
    .useReactNative() // add all built-in react native plugins
    .connect(); // let's connect!

e em app / _layout.tsx (pois esse é o nosso index):
    if (__DEV__) {
    require("../ReactotronConfig");
    }

Mas sempre fazer seguindo a documentação
